  (uuid_generate_v4(), 'vintage-hand-made-native-american-navajo-sterling-turquoise-earrings-by-alvin-to', '4345093504', 'https://www.etsy.com/listing/4345093504/vintage-hand-made-native-american-navajo?click_key=d2bda76a-4a38-4ad8-9367-8aa2f8800d1e%3ALTb2072f12d519e55d20ee292287fdbf83a46b02be&click_sum=0d37c0bc&ls=s&ga_order=most_relevant&ga_search_type=all&ga_view_type=gallery&ga_search_query=turquoise+jewelry&ref=search_grid-563634-18-7&sr_prefetch=1&pf_from=search&pro=1&sts=1&content_source=d2bda76a-4a38-4ad8-9367-8aa2f8800d1e%253ALTb2072f12d519e55d20ee292287fdbf83a46b02be',
   'Vintage Hand Made Native American Navajo Sterling Turquoise Earrings by Alvin Todacheene – First Man & First Woman', 'Up for your consideration is this extraordinary pair of vintage Navajo earrings crafted by the talented silversmith Alvin Todacheene, dated circa 1970. Each piece is beautifully handmade in sterling silver and set with a vibrant turquoise cabochon, showcasing remarkable craftsmanship and deep cultural symbolism. These unique earrings are designed in a rectangular arched shape, finely etched with detailed hand-stamped patterns resembling traditional motifs. They each feature a smooth, domed turquoise stone placed at the top, representing balance and harmony. What makes these earrings truly special is the individualized stamping on the reverse side. One earring is inscribed with "FIRST MAN", while the other reads "FIRST WOMAN", symbolizing a sacred balance and the deep cultural heritage of the Diné (Navajo) people. Both are stamped “HAND MADE”, “STERLING”, and clearly signed Todacheene along with his hallmark. These earrings measure approximately 2 inches long by 3/4 inches wide and are clip-on style. A bold and meaningful collector’s piece, perfect for admirers of Native American artistry and heritage jewelry.', 'turquoise-jewelry',
