  (uuid_generate_v4(), 'old-stock-ithaca-peak-turquoise-cabochon-round-arizona-kingman-gemstone-21-2-mm-', '4512233071', 'https://www.etsy.com/listing/4512233071/ithaca-peak-turquoise-cabochon-arizona?click_key=d2bda76a-4a38-4ad8-9367-8aa2f8800d1e%3ALT88ea7c70adbce90c815606d163a6d6be72e9848e&click_sum=850ba5f5&ls=s&ga_order=most_relevant&ga_search_type=all&ga_view_type=gallery&ga_search_query=turquoise+jewelry&ref=search_grid-563634-18-6&sr_prefetch=1&pf_from=search&cns=1&sts=1&content_source=d2bda76a-4a38-4ad8-9367-8aa2f8800d1e%253ALT88ea7c70adbce90c815606d163a6d6be72e9848e',
   'Old Stock Ithaca Peak Turquoise Cabochon: Round Arizona Kingman Gemstone (21.2 mm, 15.9 carats)', 'This old stock Arizona Ithaca Peak Turquoise cabochon is a round gemstone, 21.2 mm, weighing 15.9 carats. The cabochon has an approximate 4.0 mm dome (total height) and a 2.3 mm girdle (side height), making it ideal for a professional bezel setting. The turquoise has been professionally stabilized like most turquoise from the area. Ithaca Peak Turquoise is a highly collectible variety of Kingman Turquoise sourced from the historic Mineral Park mining district outside of Kingman, Arizona. This classic American locality is celebrated for its vivid blue colors and heavy inclusions of iron pyrite. This cabochon was cut from old stock rough salvaged from this legendary claim, an area that no longer produces this material. The cabochon features vivid turquoise blue interspersed with mirrored iron pyrite and translucent light grey quartz. The stone consists of solid, stabilized turquoise and matrix with no backing material, remaining structurally sound. It has a flat back and a straight girdle designed specifically for custom metalsmithing. Due to the natural crystalline growth of iron pyrite and quartz alongside turquoise, tiny natural vugs, hairline fractures or micro pockets are present where these different minerals meet on the face. These minor variations in texture are normal for pyrite turquoise, and the face has been well polished to a bright luster. Turquoise is a December birthstone, 11th anniversary gemstone and the State Gemstone of Arizona. Metaphysically, turquoise is considered one of the most powerful healing stones. Throughout history different cultures, including Native Americans, Tibetans and Egyptians, revered its healing powers. Turquoise is said to be a stone of communication and helps the mental state overall by increasing serenity, creativity, empathy, positive thinking, intuition, happiness and wisdom. It is considered a stone of friendship. Its blue color has come to symbolize the spirit or sky. Listing Photo Note: The photos were taken outside in', 'accessories',
